5.  World Animal Protection, "5 ways turkeys suffer on factory farms" — birth to slaughter in under five months; leg and joint pain from rapid growth.
6.  McGeown et al., "Effect of carprofen on lameness in broiler chickens," Veterinary Record, 1999 — carprofen, a painkiller commonly prescribed for dogs, sharply improved walking in lame fast-growing chickens, evidence that walking hurts them. See also Danbury et al., "Self-selection of the analgesic drug carprofen by lame broiler chickens", 2000, in which lame birds chose painkiller-laced feed.
7.  Lewis & Clark Law School, "Let's Talk Turkey: The Law Fails To Provide Even Basic Protections To Birds Used For Food" — shackling, electrified-water stunning, and throat-cutting blades; 99.8% of U.S. turkeys raised on factory farms.
8.  Mercy For Animals, "Tell the USDA It's Time to End the Torture" — citing the USDA estimate that about 1 million birds a year are scalded alive.
9.  USDA National Agricultural Library, "Humane Methods of Slaughter Act" — the Act covers livestock but not poultry. USDA says poultry are instead handled under the Poultry Products Inspection Act, which has no stunning requirement.
10.  The Tyee, "If Animals Are Conscious, What About Us?" — quotes the 2024 New York Declaration on Animal Consciousness, which states there is "strong scientific support" for conscious experience in mammals and birds. Some scientists argue the declaration overstates the evidence, especially for birds.
11.  Sentience Institute, "US Factory Farming Estimates" — an estimated 99% of U.S. farmed animals live on factory farms (a figure driven mostly by chickens).
12.  UC Davis Center for Animal Welfare, "Proposition 12 FAQs about Pigs" — gestation crates are typically 7 by 2 feet; a 2012 USDA survey found most large-herd U.S. sows housed in them.
13.  USDA Agricultural Marketing Service, Egg Markets Overview — U.S. table-egg hens are now roughly 54% caged and 46% cage-free (cage-free hens live in crowded barns). USDA APHIS, "Colostrum Feeding and Management on U.S. Dairy Operations, 1991–2014" — in 2014, 71.5% of dairy operations separated calves from their mothers less than 12 hours after birth.
14.  Our World in Data, "More than 80 billion land animals are slaughtered for meat every year" — 83 billion in 2022.
15.  Our World in Data, "How many animals get slaughtered every day?" — about 202 million chickens per day (2021), or roughly 2,340 per second.
16.  Mood & Brooke, "Estimating global numbers of fishes caught from the wild annually from 2000 to 2019," Animal Welfare, 2024 — 1.1–2.2 trillion wild fish caught per year; most are not stunned.
